   112	prompt_header() {
   113	cat <<PROMPT
   114	You are the cross-vendor reviewer on the 24h release hold (ADR-103) for
   115	the GA promotion of $RC_TAG to v1.3.0. Be adversarial and concrete.
   116	Your output is advisory evidence, not an authorization. The scope is
   117	SPLIT in 2 payloads (redactor cap); this is payload $1/2: $2.
   118	Each part is judged independently; GA needs GO on both.
   119	
   120	CONTEXT
   121	- Repo: ceo-orchestration, a governance/auditability framework. Python
   122	  stdlib-only, >=3.9. No speed claims anywhere.
   123	- $RC_TAG is CUT, signed, CI-green, published as a GitHub pre-release,
   124	  under a signed pair-rail verdict (GO-WITH-CONDITIONS).
   125	- Review history you must NOT re-litigate: 4 pre-rc.1 rounds (18
   126	  findings, 17 fixed 1 refuted) + 4 multi-part rounds rc.1->rc.2
   127	  (all real findings cured in fix-forwards) + the FIRST hold re-pass
   128	  (over rc.2, 2026-08-10) which returned NO-GO with 8 real findings -
   129	  ALL cured in rc.3 (CHANGELOG counts+upgrade section, scoped header
   130	  matcher, checklist sites, npm-publish tag-liveness guard, release-gate
   131	  timeout 20->35) and the cure diff itself passed a codex rail to GO
   132	  (evidence: repass-rc3-cures/). Verify the cures HOLD at this tag;
   133	  do not re-report them as new findings unless one is WRONG or
   134	  incomplete.
   135	- FOUR NAMED PRODUCT EXCEPTIONS ride this GA by signed decision
   136	  (V1/V2/V4/V5 - upgrade.sh observer w/o baseline-invalid guard; false
   137	  --pin NOTE; rejected-symlink hash fallthrough; FMS_LINK_PATHS unset
   138	  allow-all on install). Cures are STAGED in a post-GA ceremony pack.
   139	  Do NOT report these as new; DO report if any is WORSE than described
   140	  or reachable on the mainline install/upgrade path (they were assessed
   141	  as non-mainline).
   142	- OWN-0016 is a known gated defect (ADR-190 s2.6, expected nightly RED).
   143	
   144	WHAT THIS HOLD RE-PASS IS FOR
   145	1. GA EXECUTABILITY: remaining path is bump --stable (expected no-op),
   146	   tag --stable, push (push triggers npm publish via OIDC). Anything
   147	   non-idempotent or order-dependent?
   148	2. IRREVERSIBILITY: what lands wrong on npm and cannot be undone?
   149	   Version-string disagreement across published surfaces is the
   150	   highest-value class.
   151	3. ADOPTER BLAST RADIUS: v1.2.0 adopter runs the documented upgrade
   152	   against v1.3.0 - broken/locked states?
   153	4. HONESTY OF CLAIMS: every count/guarantee in the changed docs must
   154	   match the code at the tag. A gate that cannot fail is a finding.
   155	5. What a reviewer would most plausibly have missed across 8 rounds.
   156	
   157	OUTPUT FORMAT
   158	Per finding: SEVERITY (P0 blocks GA / P1 fix before GA / P2 follow-up),
   159	FILE:LINE, concrete failure scenario, minimal fix. Cite the diff.
   160	End with exactly one line: "VERDICT: GO" or "VERDICT: NO-GO" or
   161	"VERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS", plus one sentence. A clean round is a
   162	legitimate result - do not manufacture findings.
   163	
   164	UNIFIED DIFF ($BASE_TAG..$RC_TAG, part $1/2) FOLLOWS.
   165	PROMPT
   166	}
   167	
   168	# Tentativa COMPLETA anterior (manifesto valido + RUNNER-OVERALL) NAO e
   169	# apagada por rerun (rail r26 P1-1): um NO-GO integro exige triagem e
   170	# arquivamento explicito antes de nova tentativa - um GO posterior nao
   171	# pode simplesmente superar um NO-GO sem cura.
   172	if [ -f "$OUT/MANIFEST-ga.sha256" ] \
   173	   && ( cd "$OUT" && shasum -a 256 -c MANIFEST-ga.sha256 --status ) 2>/dev/null \
   174	   && grep -qE "^RUNNER-OVERALL: rc=" "$OUT/PROVENANCE-ga.md" 2>/dev/null; then
   175	  echo "FATAL: evidencia COMPLETA de tentativa anterior presente em repass-ga/"
   176	  echo "  (RUNNER-OVERALL: $(grep -E '^RUNNER-OVERALL:' "$OUT/PROVENANCE-ga.md" | tail -1))"
   177	  echo "  Se foi NO-GO: triagem + arquivamento (mv para repass-ga-<data>-NOGO/) antes de re-rodar."
   178	  echo "  Se foi GO: o OWNER-GA-CUT reusa - nao re-rode o runner."
