Concrete failure scenario: the scripts rail pins `SCRIPTS-MANIFEST.sha256`, but nothing checked inside that evidence binds it to the current `CEREMONY-MANIFEST.sha256`. A self-consistent GO directory from an earlier script revision can therefore be paired with newly regenerated ceremony/product manifests and pass as current review evidence.  
Minimal fix: include manifest-pinned scripts provenance containing the current ceremony-manifest SHA, verify that binding here, and enforce contiguous per-round payload/diff/transcript/verdict tuples.

